cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "uyghur-normalizer: 2009/2011 imla orthographic and de-calquing normalization for Uyghur"
message: "If you use this software or its map data, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: UyghurReferenceTexts
    website: "https://github.com/UyghurReferenceTexts"
repository-code: "https://github.com/UyghurReferenceTexts/uyghur-normalizer"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free normalizer for Uyghur text in the Arabic script. Applies
  three ordered passes: terminology calqued from Chinese, pre-2009 spellings,
  and loanword shape under the 2009/2011 orthographic reform. Suffixes are
  re-derived against the replacement with vowel harmony, voicing assimilation
  and raising, and the tool declines rather than guesses where the derivation
  is not safe. Includes the map data, arbitrated word by word against the 2011
  imla dictionary of the Milletler Til-Yeziq Komiteti.
keywords:
  - Uyghur
  - orthography
  - imla
  - text normalization
  - low-resource languages
  - machine translation
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/UyghurReferenceTexts/uyghur-normalizer/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-17"
